WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.620
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday.
So every January I write myself two letters:

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.380
one looking back at the year that was and
one setting a series of goals for the year to come.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.620
And over the last 10 years, these letters
have become a big deal to me.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:16.600
They help me to reflect and also to try to
make conscious choices about my life.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.840
And they've also helped me to achieve lots of goals,
from running half marathons to writing novels.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.040
But this year I'm thinking about
the letters a little differently.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:30.660
I'm focusing on beginnings and endings: what do I want
to begin and what do I want to end or finish.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:31.900
Let's start there!

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.920
So first, this year I will finish our Crash Course in
European history, which has been great fun

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.120
and has taught me so much about how to
shift perspectives when studying history.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.200
But it is going to end because
we are approaching the present.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.220
And also there are a couple other creative
projects I'd like to wrap up this year,

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.420
but I can't talk about those publicly yet.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.460
Most importantly in 2020, I would like to finish
raising the $20 million that Partners in Health

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.680
needs in order to break ground on the Maternal
Center of Excellence, which will dramatically improve

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:02.660
the healthcare options available to
women and children in Sierra Leone.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:09.560
Thousands of you have become monthly donors to that
project at PIH.org/hankandjohn, and I am so grateful.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.360
And so are people in Sierra Leone of course,
one of whom made me this amazing artwork.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.520
But we still need to raise a few million dollars,
which I realize is a lot of money.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.420
And maybe 2020 isn't a realistic goal for it,
but it's my goal.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:26.300
By the way, if you can make a big donation to Partners in
Health, please email me at sparksflyup@gmail.com

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.060
or just donate directly to the matching fund.
There is a link in the doobly-doo.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:36.640
The last thing I want to finish is writing a book.
Not necessarily a novel, but some kind of book.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.940
Alright, onto beginnings.
I would like to begin

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.079
no longer working at night or on the
weekends, which I guess is also a way of

00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:46.979
saying I would like to end the practice
of working at night or on the weekends,

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:51.540
which makes me think that in some ways, every new
beginning leads to some other beginning's end,

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.280
but now I'm quoting the band Semisonic
by way of the stoic philosopher Seneca.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.660
We've got to get out of this tailspin!
Mayday! Mayday!

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:02.960
Right, to keep this goal specific, measurable,
and achievable, I want to work no more than

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:07.260
one night per week and never on the weekends,
except for when I'm traveling for work,

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:12.800
like this weekend when I will be in St. Petersburg,
Atlanta, and Raleigh on tour with Hank. Come see us!

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.560
I think on of those shows is sold out, but come see
us at the other ones! Links in the doobly-doo.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.600
A very exciting beginning: Sarah's book You Are an Artist
comes out in April, and the galleys are here!

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:25.800
It's a wonderful collection of art assignments
and creativity prompts with lots of art history.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:29.980
It's just so great, and I'm so excited!
And it's available for pre-order now.

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:35.080
Also Hank, your book A Beautifully Foolish Endeavor,
which is SUCH a good title, comes out in July.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:40.320
And I will be touring with both you and Sarah in the
hopes of helping those books have good beginnings.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.100
So a lot of travel this year, which means I gotta take
good care of my body and my brain,

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.640
which is part of my body.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:49.880
Slightly off topic, but what a weird thing
it is to have a mind made out of body.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:53.580
Last beginning: I would like to write one
thank-you note every day for the entire year.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:56.340
I did this for a month back in November,
and it helped me so much!

00:02:56.340 --> 00:03:00.780
It made me feel more grateful and less pessimistic.
I got the idea from an 82 year old woman

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.960
who wrote me a thank-you note and explained
the project that she was doing,

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.980
but then I lost her address
so I can't thank her back.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.340
So... maybe she's watching!
Thank you.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.720
There are also several things I don't want
to begin or end

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:15.780
but instead want to continue,
like exercising at least 150 minutes per week,

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:19.280
making Dear Hank and John every Monday,
making a Vlogbrothers video every Tuesday,

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.260
and not losing large swaths of my life to scrolling
through Twitter as dread washes over me.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.740
I'm curious what you'd like to
begin, end, and continue in 2020

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:32.520
and what you see when you look back at your 2019.
So let's continue the conversation in comments.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.900
Before I go, one thing I hope
you will begin this year:

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:38.480
the Nerdfighteria Census,
which is so, so helpful to us

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:43.980
in determining the priorities of our community
and what you would like us to do together.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:47.220
You can find a link to it in the doobly-doo
and in the comments below.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:50.900
Hank, it is a great pleasure to say
in a third decade:

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:52.700
I will see you on Friday.

